### PayFlow Lab — example requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP)
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Create a payment (new -> 201)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ORDER-837463

{
  "merchantId": "MERCHANT_001",
  "amount": 49900,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "paymentMethod": "card",
  "customer": { "email": "test@example.com" }
}

### Replay the SAME idempotency key + body (-> 200, same paymentId)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ORDER-837463

{
  "merchantId": "MERCHANT_001",
  "amount": 49900,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "paymentMethod": "card",
  "customer": { "email": "test@example.com" }
}

### Reuse the key with a DIFFERENT body (-> 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ORDER-837463

{
  "merchantId": "MERCHANT_001",
  "amount": 10000,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "paymentMethod": "card"
}

### NGN routes to Paystack
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantId": "MERCHANT_002",
  "amount": 250000,
  "currency": "NGN",
  "paymentMethod": "card"
}

### Fetch a payment (replace with a real reference)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/payments/PAY_847293

### Timeline
GET {{base}}/api/v1/payments/PAY_847293/timeline

### --- Phase 2: simulation + stats ---

### Start a bulk simulation (1000 payments at 200/s) -> 202 with runId
POST {{base}}/api/v1/simulation/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactions": 1000,
  "transactionsPerSecond": 200
}

### Poll a run (replace with the returned runId)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/simulation/SIM_xxxxxxxx

### List all runs
GET {{base}}/api/v1/simulation

### Aggregate stats overview
GET {{base}}/api/v1/stats

### --- Phase 3: webhooks ---

### Forged webhook (bad signature) -> expect 401
POST {{base}}/webhooks/stripe
Content-Type: application/json
stripe-signature: t=1,v1=deadbeef

{
  "id": "evt_forged",
  "type": "payment_intent.succeeded",
  "data": { "object": { "id": "pi_x" } }
}

# NOTE: valid webhooks are delivered automatically by the fake PSP after you
# create a payment. Create one, wait ~3s, then GET its /timeline to see
# WEBHOOK_RECEIVED -> WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_VERIFIED -> PAYMENT_CONFIRMED.
# To find payments stuck in `pending`, look at /stats after a simulation drains.

### --- Phase 4: REAL Paystack checkout (needs PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY in .env) ---

### Start a real checkout -> returns authorizationUrl (open it, pay with a test card)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantId": "MERCHANT_001",
  "amount": 500000,
  "currency": "NGN",
  "customer": { "email": "buyer@example.com" }
}

### Manually verify a checkout (replace with the returned paymentId)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/checkout/PAY_xxxxxx/verify

### --- Phase 5: routing & retries ---

### View routing config + live provider health
GET {{base}}/api/v1/routing

### Switch to performance-based routing
POST {{base}}/api/v1/routing
Content-Type: application/json

{ "strategy": "performance" }

### Switch to weighted routing
POST {{base}}/api/v1/routing
Content-Type: application/json

{ "strategy": "weighted" }

### EUR is stripe-only (capability constraint) — create a few and check provider
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "M1", "amount": 20000, "currency": "EUR", "paymentMethod": "card" }

### NGN never routes to stripe (only paystack/flutterwave)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "merchantId": "M1", "amount": 20000, "currency": "NGN", "paymentMethod": "card" }

### --- Phase 6: reconciliation ---
# Tip: run a simulation first, wait ~12s, then reconcile a SHORT window so you
# only compare freshly-generated data (older txns predate the PSP ledger).

### Run reconciliation over the last 3 minutes
POST {{base}}/api/v1/reconciliation/run
Content-Type: application/json

{ "windowMinutes": 3 }

### List reconciliation runs
GET {{base}}/api/v1/reconciliation

### View a run's findings (replace with the returned runId)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/reconciliation/1

### --- Phase 8: faults, incidents, log search ---

### Inject a fault (expire stripe credentials)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/faults
Content-Type: application/json

{ "provider": "stripe", "authError": true }

### View active faults
GET {{base}}/api/v1/faults

### Clear a provider's faults
DELETE {{base}}/api/v1/faults/stripe

### Start an incident drill (root cause hidden)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/incidents/start

### Resolve an incident (reveals root cause, lifts fault) — replace id
POST {{base}}/api/v1/incidents/INC_xxxxxxxx/resolve

### Log search: failed PSP responses on stripe in the last 15 min
GET {{base}}/api/v1/events?type=PSP_RESPONSE_RECEIVED&provider=stripe&sinceMinutes=15

### Log search: everything for one payment
GET {{base}}/api/v1/events?reference=PAY_123456
